2026-09-27 — read-only KVM instruction-count diagnosis, NOT acceptance.

Four diagnostic flights pass: demand/reference, demand/subject,
memslot/reference, memslot/subject. Each reuses its matching retained
Image/System.map, the existing 256-KiB one-mode ftrace payload, and the same
64-MiB snapshot scratch disk. No installed object, Image, payload, production
QEMU or kernel contract is changed. KASLR is disabled only in this diagnostic.
The private matching-version QEMU's opt-in store intervention is disabled.

The API-7 plugin instruments instruction entry, including a faulting
instruction's entry, using per-vCPU counters. Nonoverlapping symbol ranges
count aliases once and stop at every intervening symbol, including data.
The recorded numbers are whole-boot totals in selected ranges, NOT elapsed
time or workload-only counts. Inlining changes attribution: an absent GCC
helper is not zero-cost execution, and different child call counts must not
be normalized as if their paths were identical. Boot-time page-free totals
are explicitly not evidence of the original KVM workload's cost.

Each flight exits zero with the diagnostic TAP result and ordered nonce-bound
boot/shutdown; all input hashes, including scratch, remain unchanged. Independent
ftrace confirms 87 demand fault-handler entries on each kernel, and four
stage-2 destructions plus two memslot invalidations on each memslot flight.
The memslot runner enforces this independently. The earlier demand receipts
predate that added assertion; its retained logs also satisfy the same check.

                           demand: GCC       EvoCC     memslot: GCC      EvoCC
__kvm_pgtable_walk insns          165950      121550           166140     129078
                  entries           366         366              368        368
__kvm_pgtable_visit insns        inlined      890711          inlined     960033
                   entries                   3560                         3834
kvm_handle_guest_abort insns      25797      119638            25797     119638
                       entries       87          87               87         87
stage2_free_walker insns           35840       84480            35840      84480
                  entries          2560        2560             2560       2560
kvm_free_stage2_pgd insns            136         440              136        440
                   entries            4           4                4          4

These measurements identify code-generation overhead for further reduction;
they do not prove that visitor inlining alone closes the original 120-second,
all-mode K02/K03 tests. The bounded compiler repair has its separate record in
recursive-inline-visitor.out. A fresh complete Image and original tests remain
required. Instrumented times must never be compared to acceptance times.

Reproduce with tests/fixtures/kvm-instruction-count.py; each result.json retains
the exact argv, nonce, input paths/hashes and serial/instruction-log hashes.
